PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
Due to the New Years holiday, a meeting of the Public Services Committee was instead held on
Wednesday, January 3, 2024, in Committee Room 104 and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:01
p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Bryan Cook, Chairman, Pete Laybourn, and Tom Segrave. Absent:
Dr. Rinne.
AGENDA ITEMS
7.
ORDINANCE
—3
READING
—
Amending
subsection
6.7.5.b
of the
Unified
Development Code (UDC), changing building façade design requirements to reduce
required windows on urban loft multifamily residential and mixed-use residential
development. (POSTPONED FROM DECEMBER 21, 2023)
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on 3” and final reading, seconded by Mr. Layboum. Mr. Segrave
moved to amend by substitute dated December 21, 2023, seconded by Mr. Layboum. Motion to
amend failed with Mr. Segrave voting “YES” and Mr. Layboum voting “NO”. Main motion failed
with Mr. Segrave voting “YES” and Mr. Layboum voting “NO”.
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department Senior Planner, provided a staff report.
Committee member Segrave commcnted on the item and public comments were made by Brenda
Birkie, My Front Door, and Chair of the Affordable Housing Taskforce, and Ansley Mouw,
Winters Griffith Architects.
Ii.
ORDINANCE
READING
— Amending Title 6, Animals, of the Municipal Code of
the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, regarding the registration, control, impoundment and
general care of animals and birds within the city. (POSTPONED FROM DECEMBER21,
2023)
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on 2 reading, seconded by Mr. Layboum. Mr. Segrave moved to
amend by substitute dated January 2, 2024, seconded by Mr. Laybourn, Motion to amend failed
with Mr. Segrave voting “YES” and Mr. Layboum voting “NO”.
Main motion failed by
unanimous voice vote.
John Brodie, Deputy City Attorney, provided a staff report and provided a proposed substitute.
Elizabeth Wagner, Animal Control, provided additional information. Chainnan Cook and
committee members Layboum and Segrave commented on the item. Public comments were made
by Amber Ash, Cheyenne Animal Shelter Director of Strategic Initiatives, and Janet Stephens,
Cheyenne Kennel Club.
13.
ORDINANCE •3rd READING
— Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, land
located east of Polk Avenue and north of and adjacent to East Pershing Boulevard.
